= Consumer Responsibilities & Quality Certification Marks

Statutory rights remain ineffective without active, vigilant consumer responsibility.

== The Ten Cardinal Consumer Responsibilities (NCERT)
1. *Market Awareness:* Exercising awareness regarding the price, quality, warranty, and terms of available goods and services.
2. *Purchasing Standardized Goods:* Buying only goods with accredited national quality marks (ISI, AGMARK, Hallmark).
3. *Following Usage Instructions:* Reading product manuals and operating dangerous appliances with proper care.
4. *Insisting on a Cash Memo:* Demanding and preserving the *Cash Memo*, which constitutes indispensable documentary evidence in consumer courts.
5. *Asserting Rights:* Exercising vigilance to secure fair commercial terms without timid compromise.
6. *Honesty in Dealings:* Refusing to purchase smuggled goods, counterfeit items, or participating in black marketing.
7. *Filing Legitimate Complaints:* Initiating formal complaints before consumer commissions even when monetary losses are minor, deterring rogue businesses.
8. *Forming Consumer Advocacy Societies:* Organizing local community consumer forums to champion public interests.
9. *Environmental Responsibility:* Respecting ecological balance by avoiding single-use plastics, minimizing litter, and choosing green products.
10. *Critical Scrutiny of Advertising:* Refusing to be misled by exaggerated celebrity endorsements or deceptive promotional gimmicks.

